# CAMBER: the hover racer, at the game's own defaults (RATE 60 FPS, track
# LAGOON, class BRISK, mode RACE). Run with --boot off --fps 60
# --frames 1251.
#
# Home screen: one step right to the CAMBER tile.
90 press right
91 release right
# A (south) at 110 opens the game. The title menu stays up with its
# live race behind it until 690.
110 press south
111 release south
# DOWN (250) to TRACK, then RIGHT three times: FURNACE (300), GLACIER
# (400) and round to LAGOON again (500); each change starts the live
# scene behind the menu on that track. UP (620) back to PLAY.
250 press down
251 release down
300 press right
301 release right
400 press right
401 release right
500 press right
501 release right
620 press up
621 release up
# A on PLAY starts the race and stays held from here on as the
# throttle. The lights count down; GO! shows at about 870.
# (PLAY is pressed at 690 on purpose: with this timing the race runs the
# same as one started right away, so the lines below stay valid.)
690 press south
# From 891 the ship drives itself by these lines: every 4 pictures the
# stick points at the middle of the road seen on two rows, and B (east),
# the air brake, is pulled when the road runs far off to one side. A
# closed-loop helper wrote these lines by looking at each picture; they
# are plain inputs and replay the same race every time.
# About 930: the opening straight with the rivals ahead.
# About 939 to 980: the first right bend, with the air brake.
891 stick left -10290 0
891 press south
